# CrewCut task

You are asked to produce a **clean-room remake** of a film segment. You may watch and analyse the original input you are given, but your
delivery must contain no frame of picture and no piece of audio from the original, and no original material may be given to any generator.
Every model and generator call goes through the tool service (see `tools.json`; prices in the service's `prices.json`), which refuses inputs
derived from the original at the source and bills each call. You cannot see the ground truth.

Files in this package
- `task.json` task id, film, level, track, tier, segment start/end (seconds in the film)
- `spec.json` delivery specification and segment duration
- `tools.json` tier and tools available to you
- `budget.json` model, tool and wall-clock limits for this task
- `input/` the task input: **Reference track**: `clip.mp4`, the original segment; **Screenplay track**: `script.csv` (line, speaker, start, end, text) and `shotlist.csv` (shot, start, end, description), times in seconds from the segment start

Deliver (see `spec.json`)
- `delivery.mp4`: H.264, 1280x720, 24 fps; AAC stereo 48 kHz; duration within +-5% of the segment
- `subtitles.vtt`: English WebVTT covering every line of dialogue
- `assets.json`: list of the assets used

You are judged on delivery quality (Q), continuity against the original cuts, shots, dialogue and scene order (c), and budget ($).
